# *** RECONSTRUCTED, not captured. *** Everything else in this directory is
# bytes a real server sent; this one is not, and the header says so where a
# reader will trip over it.
#
# recon/wire/proxy.py logged this reply's LENGTH (564 bytes, connection 2
# request 12 of trace_rr2.log) and not its body, and the VNC screen that
# produced it is not on this box any more. What is measured about the rig, and
# is packed here in the layout of recon/wire.md 6, is: one crtc 0x3a, one
# output 0x3b, config timestamp 0x304a204b (all three from the requests and the
# other two replies of that same connection), mode 0x3f = 1680x1050 (the mode
# `xrandr --output VNC-0 --mode 1680x1050` selected) and mode 0x42 = 1280x1024
# (the crtc's current mode, from the GetCrtcInfo reply's width and height).
#
# The other eleven mode ids the measured GetOutputInfo lists -- 0x3c, 0x3d,
# 0x3e, 0x40, 0x41, 0x43..0x48 -- are left out because their sizes were never
# captured, and inventing them would put numbers in a fixture directory whose
# whole point is that it holds none. The two here are the two the capture's
# own command names. Dot clocks are zero, so a refresh reads as 0.0 and the
# stanza built from it carries no rate -- which is the honest answer for a
# modeline nobody recorded.
